# Specification: README skill integration

Authorized scope: locally install and adapt the supplied skill and SDD bridge,
update actual consumers, preserve existing changes and verify integration.
No application implementation or general documentation rewrite is authorized.

- REQ-01: The complete portable skill and configured bridge retain meaningful resource routing and remove imported product-specific mandates.
- AC-01 → REQ-01: Installed entry, metadata, resources and bridge have valid identities/links; every archive member is accounted for and adaptations are explicit.
- REQ-02: Catalog, versioned profile and bridge inventory agree without weakening selection or existing specialization gates.
- AC-02 → REQ-02: Thirty-one entries and bridges agree; missing/extra/unreviewed resources and mutations are rejected.
- REQ-03: Historical records and workspace changes remain recoverable by exact bytes.
- AC-03 → REQ-03: Registered successors recover exact predecessors; corrupt, missing, escaping or unregistered inputs fail, including independent distribution.
- REQ-04: Current reader navigation and claims match repository authorities.
- AC-04 → REQ-04: Counts, skill-selection boundary and README F0 status agree with actual files/evidence; focused and applicable governance checks pass, with limits recorded.

These are library/integration criteria, not proof of improved reader usability,
external scientific claims or new product runtime acceptance. No AGENTS policy
expansion, global installation, commit or publication is required.

## Authorized README preservation repair — 2026-11-04

The maintainer's subsequent “corrija” authorizes repair of the reported README
preservation failure after the documentation rewrite. Extend REQ-03/04 with one
exact README successor: recover the original integration bytes, reject unknown
current bytes and malformed/missing/escaping registry resources, and verify the
independent governance copy. This supersedes the original no-general-rewrite scope
only for the previously requested documentation and this bounded repair. No product
code, profile, historical digest, criterion or publication scope changes.
